{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And the pit was empty, there was no water in it.</b> Rashi explained: there was no water in it, but there were snakes and scorpions in it. The explanation is that רק and אין do not constitute a limitation after a limitation, and אין מא\"ם but rather to include, to say that there was something in it. And if you ask: from where does he know that it was snakes? Say it was stones in it. One can answer: from the fact that it writes רק, it implies a thing from which it would sometimes be emptied."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:32.393791618Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}